{% comment %}
  Request a Corporate Gifting Quote (Figma: 508:12153, and 508:12683 for the state
  after it is sent).

  Two states in one section, because they are two states of one thing rather than
  two sections a merchant has to remember to swap: the form, and the panel that
  replaces it once the request is in. Shopify decides which, not a setting and not
  a script — `{% form 'contact' %}` posts to the shop, redirects back with
  `?contact_posted=true`, and `form.posted_successfully?` is true on that render.
  So the confirmation survives a reload, works with JavaScript off, and cannot be
  reached by anyone who has not actually sent anything.

  The seven fields are a fixed composition rather than a merchant's list — the
  layout is drawn around two columns of them and a quote needs the answers it
  needs — so they are the section's, with their labels as the file writes them.
  What a merchant does change is exposed: the gift types on offer, the minimum on
  the quantity field, and every word of the confirmation, which is blocks.

  The whole form lives in a 630 column centred in the page, which is half the
  1280 content width. That is narrow on purpose: a quote form with its fields
  stretched over a desktop's full width reads as a chore.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign gift_types = section.settings.gift_types
  assign quantity_hint = section.settings.quantity_hint
  assign submit_label = section.settings.submit_label | default: 'Submit request'
-%}

<div
  class="section section--page-width spacing-style color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}"
  style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}"
  data-testid="corporate-quote-form-{{ section.id }}"
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- form 'contact', class: 'corporate-quote' -%}
    {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
      <div class="corporate-quote__confirmation">
        <span class="corporate-quote__sparkle" aria-hidden="true">
          {{- 'icon-ui-sparkle.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
        </span>

        <div class="corporate-quote__confirmation-content">
          {% content_for 'block', type: '_ui-heading', id: 'success-heading' %}
          {% content_for 'block', type: '_ui-text', id: 'success-copy' %}
          {% content_for 'block', type: '_ui-link-row', id: 'success-buttons' %}
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      {% content_for 'blocks' %}

      {%- comment -%}
        Shopify reports a failed post through `form.errors`, and the only field it
        validates itself is the email. Its message is put on that field so the
        error lands where the fix is, rather than in a banner above a form the
        visitor then has to search.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign email_error = blank
        if form.errors
          assign email_error = form.errors.messages.email | default: form.errors.messages.form
        endif
      -%}

      <div class="corporate-quote__grid">
        {% render 'ui-input',
          label: 'Name',
          name: 'contact[name]',
          value: form.name
        %}

        {% render 'ui-input',
          label: 'Email',
          type: 'email',
          name: 'contact[email]',
          value: form.email,
          error: email_error,
          required: true
        %}

        {% render 'ui-input',
          label: 'Company',
          name: 'contact[Company]'
        %}

        {% render 'ui-input',
          label: 'Estimated quantity',
          type: 'number',
          name: 'contact[Estimated quantity]',
          hint: quantity_hint
        %}

        {% render 'ui-input',
          label: 'Preferred delivery date',
          name: 'contact[Preferred delivery date]',
          mask: 'MM/DD/YYYY'
        %}

        {% render 'ui-select',
          label: 'Gift type',
          name: 'contact[Gift type]',
          placeholder: section.settings.gift_type_placeholder,
          options: gift_types
        %}

        <div class="corporate-quote__wide">
          {% render 'ui-input',
            label: 'Notes or recipient needs',
            textarea: true,
            rows: '5',
            name: 'contact[body]',
            placeholder: section.settings.notes_placeholder
          %}
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The kit's own button, not a `<button>` wearing its class names. Hand-rolled,
        it was `width: fit-content` and `margin: 0` — the snippet's own rules, which
        a section stylesheet of the same weight loses to on order alone, so the
        button came out 163 wide against the 630 the file draws and sat flush under
        the notes field. `full_width` is the switch that answers it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% render 'ui-button',
        variant: 'primary',
        label: submit_label,
        type: 'submit',
        full_width: true,
        class: 'corporate-quote__submit'
      %}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endform -%}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
   * 630 centred, whatever the page is doing around it. The section sits in the
   * `.section` grid, which already places it in the central column, so this only
   * has to narrow that column rather than pad itself — see the page geometry note
   * in CLAUDE.md.
   */
  .corporate-quote {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 630px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  /* The file leaves 48 between the heading and the first row of fields. */
  .corporate-quote > :is(.ui-heading, h1, h2, h3) {
    margin-block: 0 48px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /*
   * Two columns of 305 with a 20 gutter is exactly 630, so the columns are
   * written as fractions and the gutter as the gap — the same pair of numbers,
   * without a width that stops being true the moment the container moves.
   *
   * `align-items: start` because the quantity field is 20px taller than the one
   * beside it: it carries a hint line. Stretched, the shorter field would grow a
   * gap under its own box and the two controls would stop lining up.
   */
  .corporate-quote__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    align-items: start;
    column-gap: 20px;
    row-gap: 16px;
  }

  .corporate-quote__wide {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  /*
   * One column on a phone. The 630 column itself needs no middle tier — from
   * 750px up the content column is at least 670 wide, so the form is already at
   * the size the file draws — but two 305px fields do not fit a 390px screen.
   */
  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .corporate-quote__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }

  /* The file leaves 48 between the last field and the button, which runs full width. */
  /*
   * Weighed one class heavier than `.ui-button`, whose `margin: 0` is declared in
   * the snippet's own stylesheet and wins on order against a lone class here. The
   * width is the snippet's `full_width` rather than a figure of ours.
   */
  .corporate-quote .corporate-quote__submit {
    margin-block-start: 48px;
  }

  /* ---------- Sent ---------- */

  /*
   * The same tinted panel the hero opens the page with, so the page closes on the
   * shape it started on. Centred throughout: the file gives this one no left edge
   * to hang from.
   */
  .corporate-quote__confirmation {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 32px 24px 48px;
    border-radius: var(--ui-radius-lg, 16px);
    background-color: var(--ui-color-light-blue);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .corporate-quote__sparkle {
    display: block;
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    color: var(--ui-color-primary);
  }

  .corporate-quote__sparkle > svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  /* Star, then 80 to the heading — 112 from the panel's top edge, less the 32 the
     star occupies. */
  .corporate-quote__confirmation-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-block-start: 48px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .corporate-quote__confirmation-content > :is(.ui-heading, h1, h2, h3) {
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* The copy is drawn at 445 inside the 630 panel, so it wraps to the three lines
     the file shows rather than running the full width. */
  .corporate-quote__confirmation-content > :is(.ui-text, p) {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 445px;
  }

  /* The file leaves 48 between the copy and the pair of buttons. */
  .corporate-quote__confirmation-content > .ui-link-row {
    margin-block-start: 32px;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .corporate-quote__confirmation {
      padding-inline: 16px;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Corporate quote form",
  "tag": "section",
  "blocks": [{ "type": "_ui-heading" }, { "type": "_ui-text" }, { "type": "_ui-link-row" }],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "gift_types",
      "label": "Gift types",
      "info": "Comma separated. These are the options in the gift type field.",
      "default": "Logo treats, Gift boxes, Gift cards, Custom order"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "gift_type_placeholder",
      "label": "Gift type, empty option",
      "default": "Select gift type..."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "quantity_hint",
      "label": "Note under the quantity field",
      "default": "Minimum order setup: 25 boxes"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "notes_placeholder",
      "label": "Notes field placeholder",
      "default": "Tell us about the occasion, design theme directives, or specific requirements..."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "submit_label",
      "label": "Submit button",
      "default": "Submit request"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.colors"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:settings.color_scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "t:settings.top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 80
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "t:settings.bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 200,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 80
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Corporate quote form",
      "blocks": {
        "heading": {
          "type": "_ui-heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<h2>Request a<br><em>Corporate Gifting Quote</em></h2>"
          }
        },
        "success-heading": {
          "type": "_ui-heading",
          "static": true,
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<h2><em>Thanks.</em><br>We have your inquiry.</h2>"
          }
        },
        "success-copy": {
          "type": "_ui-text",
          "static": true,
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The Treat House team will review your order details and follow up with next steps. If your order has a firm event date, please include that in your request.</p>"
          }
        },
        "success-buttons": {
          "type": "_ui-link-row",
          "static": true,
          "blocks": {
            "primary": {
              "type": "_ui-link",
              "settings": { "label": "Shop gift cards", "variant": "primary" }
            },
            "secondary": {
              "type": "_ui-link",
              "settings": { "label": "Return home", "variant": "secondary" }
            }
          },
          "block_order": ["primary", "secondary"]
        }
      },
      "block_order": ["heading"]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
